new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..b30986efcf80336f1aeed120fe7934181a390aa7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/internal/netflow/doc.go
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+// Copyright 2020 New Relic Corporation. All rights reserved.
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
+
+// Package netflow decodes unsampled, unidirectional NetFlow version 9 records.
+// It does not decode NetFlow v5 or IPFIX, extrapolate sampled traffic, or infer
+// counters from incomplete templates. Options records and ordinary templates
+// without both addresses and both counters are structurally validated but do
+// not produce accounting records. Unknown fields are skipped by their lengths.
+// UnknownTemplates counts data FlowSets whose templates are unavailable.
+//
+// Each exporter address/port and source ID has independent state. There are at
+// most 128 such scopes, 256 templates per scope, and 128 fields per template.
+// Active capacity is not evicted by a new sender: capacity exhaustion is an
+// explicit error. Templates expire 30 minutes after their last definition;
+// data and duplicate packets do not refresh them. Idle scopes expire after
+// 30 minutes. At expiration boundaries the old state is already unavailable.
+//
+// Replay protection uses a 64-sequence-unit reorder window and the last 64
+// accepted datagram fingerprints. Repeated sequences and packets older than
+// the window are discarded without accounting. Previously unseen reordered
+// packets inside the window are accepted, but cannot replace cached templates.
+// Forward sequence wrap and uptime wrap are normal. A decreasing uptime with
+// a newer export timestamp/boot estimate resets templates and sequence state;
+// a reset to sequence zero or one also identifies an immediate reboot. As with
+// any unauthenticated UDP exporter, indistinguishable same-second restarts and
+// reordered startup packets cannot be perfectly distinguished. UNIX-second
+// precision permits two seconds of boot-estimate jitter for ordinary reordering.
+//
+// FlowSet framing, template lengths and counter widths are validated before
+// state or records are committed. Padding is limited to three zero bytes;
+// alignment is not required. Header Count is advisory, not a parsing bound:
+// softflowd 1.0.0's default v9 sender puts datagram length there and uses a
+// cumulative end-of-datagram data-record sequence. That variant is recognized
+// without guessing counter values. SequenceGaps reports missing sequence units
+// (records for that variant, datagrams for standard v9), not recovered traffic.
+package netflow
diff --git a/internal/netflow/limits_test.go b/internal/netflow/limits_test.go
